{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8efc4595ab8d0d7d43d5ec1988b1b7dc8ecc7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> diagonals. What is the measure of its exterior angle, in degrees? (An exterior angle is the supplement of an interior angle.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the number of diagonals of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4c21f0e5818daeb4d9b3ac0c7e76ccf9056b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />. Setting this expression equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8efc4595ab8d0d7d43d5ec1988b1b7dc8ecc7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dce59f6afb62825f31819ae31874cca35417bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive. The exterior angle of a regular polygon with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides in degrees is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b2fc8fad05b90c0b565950bbfbf35420d98550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dce59f6afb62825f31819ae31874cca35417bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/37807872ab225cb528673194daa6f8988bfd5030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{360}{18}=\\boxed{20^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Prob